NCCL host PUT: one-sided, stream-ordered RMA
PUT writes a peer window; the signal hands off the payload



The target rank is not involved. The source names the peer, registered window and offset; the target queues a stream wait.



 // source rank stream
                                                                                                                                                     • Unlike NVSHMEM, All NCCL Puts come with signals
 ncclPutSignal(local, count, datatype,
               peer, dst_win, offset, 0, 0, 0, comm, stream);
                                                                                                                                                     • You must pass a symmetric window into a NCCL Put
 // writes the peer window; its signal follows payload delivery                                                                                        in addition to an offset

 // destination rank stream
 ncclWaitSignal(1, &wait, comm, stream);
 // after completion, the matching payload is visible to later work




